title: Closing_Time
---
=> Red Velvet: It's 5 pm, boss! Should the girls head home?
=> Red Velvet: That's five o'clock. The girls are...erm...looking at the door. #cringe
=> Red Velvet: Five already! Home time, or are we staying late?
-> Go home. Good work today.
    => Red Velvet: Thank you, boss! See you in the morning.
    => Red Velvet: Yay! I mean...understood.
-> Stay until 8 pm. Overtime pay.
    <<overtime>>
    => Red Velvet: Well...okay. 1.25 times the usual rate, don't forget. #cringe
    => Red Velvet: The girls won't love it, but okay. Three more hours! #cringe
===
title: Day_End
---
<<if $day == 1>>
Day one is done. You made {$revenue_today}, and corporate covered the wages. That won't happen again.
<<else>>
Day {$day} is done. You made {$revenue_today} and paid {$wages_today} in wages.
<<endif>>
<<if not $milestone_today>>
    <<if $on_track>>
    Profit is sitting at {$profit}. That's already past the {$goal} corporate wants. Don't tell them, they'll raise it.
    <<elseif $days_left == 1>>
    Profit is sitting at {$profit}. Corporate wants {$goal} by tomorrow night.
    <<else>>
    Profit is sitting at {$profit}. Corporate wants {$goal} in {$days_left} more days.
    <<endif>>
<<endif>>
===
title: Day_2_Start
---
Red Velvet: Good morning, boss! Erm...just a reminder, today's the first day we're on the clock. Wages come out at the end of the day.
Red Velvet: No pressure! ...Okay, a little pressure.
===
title: Day_3_Start
---
Red Velvet: Boss, it's...erm...really hot out there today. Honey almost fainted into the dough. #cringe
Red Velvet: She says she's fine. She says the dough broke her fall.
Red Velvet: Could we get some umbrellas for the girls? It'd be about $50,000.
-> Buy the umbrellas.
    <<spend 50000>>
    <<set $umbrellas to true>>
    <<set $workers += 1>>
    Red Velvet: Thank you, boss! The girls are going to love this.
-> Sand is free. Shade isn't.
    <<set $corporate += 1>>
    Red Velvet: ...Right. I'll tell them to drink more water. We have water, right? #cringe
===
title: Day_4_Start
---
Your phone rings. You already know who it is.
Jennifer: One of your drones filed an insurance claim. Heatstroke. Something about fainting into the dough.
<<if $umbrellas>>
Jennifer: Under an umbrella. That *you* bought. I'm still reviewing that, by the way.
<<endif>>
Jennifer: Licorich has a very generous insurance policy. It covers almost nothing. Deny it.
-> Denied.
    <<set $corporate += 1>>
    Jennifer: Good. You'd be amazed how many managers get squeamish about that.
    Jennifer: You're not squeamish. I like that. ...In an employee.
-> Approve it. She fainted into a vat of dough.
    <<spend 60000>>
    <<set $workers += 1>>
    Jennifer: Fine. It's coming out of *your* bottom line, not mine. #scolding
    Red Velvet: Boss...Honey told me about the claim. Thank you. Really.
    Red Velvet: She baked you something. It's...erm...shaped like you. Mostly. #cringe
===
title: Day_7_Start
---
Red Velvet: Boss! Mocha burnt a batch of croissants this morning.
Red Velvet: She wants to know if the girls can eat the burnt ones. Nobody's going to buy them anyway.
-> Eat up. You earned it.
    <<set $workers += 1>>
    Red Velvet: Yay! Mocha's going to tell everyone you're the best boss ever. She's...erm...already telling everyone.
-> Every crumb belongs to Licorich Inc.
    <<set $corporate += 1>>
    Red Velvet: ...Even the burnt crumbs? I'll let her know. She's not going to take it well. #cringe
===
title: Day_8_Start
---
Your phone rings. You already know who it is.
Jennifer: Quick one. The board looked at your numbers and laughed. Not the good kind of laugh. #scolding
Jennifer: Mandatory overtime. Every day until the next milestone. I don't want to hear about it.
-> Consider it done.
    <<overtime_every_day true>>
    <<set $overtime_week to true>>
    <<set $corporate += 1>>
    Jennifer: Look at you, learning.
-> They're already working until they drop.
    <<set $workers += 1>>
    Jennifer: Then they can drop *after* 8 pm. ...Fine. Your funeral. Your margins, too. #scolding
===
title: Day_9_Start
---
<<if $overtime_week>>
Red Velvet: Morning, boss. The girls are...erm...tired. Honey fell asleep on the belt last night. #cringe
Red Velvet: She says it was moving, so it was like a little bed. I don't think that's how beds work.
Red Velvet: We'll manage. We always manage.
<<endif>>
===
title: Day_11_Start
---
Red Velvet: Boss? The girls asked me to ask you something. They drew straws. I lost. #cringe
Red Velvet: They were wondering about a raise. Just a little one. Everyone's wages would go up a bit every day.
-> Give everyone a raise.
    <<raise_wages 0.2>>
    <<set $workers += 1>>
    Red Velvet: Really?! Boss, you're...erm...you're the best. I'm going to go tell them. Running. I'm running now.
-> Licorich pays the market rate.
    <<set $corporate += 1>>
    Red Velvet: ...The market rate is the only rate out here, boss. There's no other market. #cringe
    <<if $corporate > $workers>>
    Your phone buzzes. A text from Corporate. Just a thumbs up. You're not sure how she knew.
    <<endif>>
===
title: Day_12_Start
---
Red Velvet: Boss, can I tell you something? Off the record?
Red Velvet: Some of the girls have been talking. About a...erm...union.
-> Tell them I'm in.
    <<set $workers += 2>>
    Red Velvet: Really?! I mean...okay! I'll let them know. Quietly.
-> Give me names.
    <<set $corporate += 2>>
    Red Velvet: ...I didn't say anything. I was talking about onions. A union of onions. #cringe
===
title: Day_13_Start
---
<<if $corporate >= 4 and not $knows_jennifer>>
Your phone rings. It's Corporate, and she sounds almost pleasant.
Jennifer: The board's been asking about you. In a good way, for once.
Jennifer: You can stop calling me Corpo-sama, by the way. It's Jennifer.
<<set $knows_jennifer to true>>
Jennifer: Don't make it weird. #scolding
<<endif>>
===
